    <section xml:id='tests-APPLICATION'>
      <title>Application Before Operators</title>
      <para>Before an operator takes the thing that follows it, that thing takes what is applied to it: a function its tuple, a value its vector literal, anything its members. So <literal>a + f(1)</literal> adds the call's result, and <literal>a + v[i]</literal> the element. A function called without parentheses takes exactly one thing; an argument that is itself a call, an indexing or a construction takes its parentheses, <literal>print(f(x))</literal>.</para>
