  <section xmlns='http://docbook.org/ns/docbook' xml:id='category-TUPLES'>
    <title>Tuples and Function Values</title>
    <para>A tuple is a value: an anonymous record written in parentheses. Its components may carry labels, and its type is written the same way, <literal>(int, String)</literal>. The empty tuple <literal>()</literal> is the type of no value, which a routine without a result answers. Functions are values too: a name bound to a function, or a method bound to its receiver, is called later like the function itself.</para>

    <section xml:id='tests-TUPLE-VALUES'>
      <title>Tuples</title>
      <para>A labelled component is read by its label. Unlabelled components are reached by decomposition, <literal>let (a, b) t</literal>; a tuple is not an array and has no indexing. A routine returns several values as a tuple.</para>
