    <section xml:id='tests-FUNCTION-VALUES'>
      <title>Functions as Values</title>
      <para><literal>let g twice</literal> binds the function at compile time and costs nothing; <literal>g(21)</literal> is a direct call. <literal>x.m</literal> without a tuple is the method bound to its receiver. Where a delegate type is declared, a named function becomes a closure value, chosen by the delegate's signature.</para>
